+/* Native 120 FPS (experimental): the open gate at twice the field rate.
+ *
+ * With the gate open a frame ends on the first VBlank after its work. Halve
+ * the VBlank period (interrupts_set_vblank_divisor) and a frame that fits in
+ * 8.3 ms ends on a 120 Hz field. The root counter the engine measures time
+ * with keeps its rate, so physics would stay right by itself - except that
+ * the quantizer rounds any frame under 19 ticks up to 17: a 120 Hz field
+ * (8.62 ticks) would be simulated as a 60 Hz one and everything would move
+ * at twice its speed. So while the fast rate is engaged, the value the
+ * quantizer stored is replaced - at the top of the next loop, before any
+ * reader - by the frame's own length in fields times 8.5 ticks: 8 and 9
+ * alternately for one field, 17 a pair, exactly the 60 Hz timeline. Two
+ * fields give 17 and four 34, as the quantizer would; three and five, which
+ * it would round up, give 25/26 and 42/43. Longer frames keep the game's
+ * own value. The length comes from the game's own stamps - the subtraction
+ * 0x80016978 feeds the quantizer - rounded to the nearest field.
+ *
+ * Three more things run per VBlank rather than per measured tick:
+ *
+ *   - the music. On NTSC libsnd uses its VSync tick mode (SsSetTickMode(1)
+ *     at 0x80033D20 becomes mode 5), and SsStart(1) chains the sequencer
+ *     tick behind libetc's VBlank handler: 0x80054E74 calls the handler it
+ *     displaced, then [0x8005EFE0]. At 120 Hz that pointer alternates
+ *     between the tick and an empty function nothing references
+ *     (0x80016EFC), switched at each VBlank edge before the guest takes
+ *     the interrupt, so the tick keeps 59.94 Hz and the tempo is unchanged.
+ *     The SsStart2 form, a VSync callback slot, is handled the same way.
+ *     The tick goes back the moment the fast rate drops;
+ *   - VSync(n) counts fields. The game only waits whole numbers of them
+ *     outside its 3D loop (VSync 5/20/60: boot, memory card, reset), so the
+ *     fast rate lasts only while the loop turns. C2_120_STALL_FIELDS fields
+ *     with no loop - a load, anything that owns the machine for a while -
+ *     drop VBlank back to NTSC from the VBlank edge itself, and
+ *     C2_120_REARM_LOOPS quick loops bring it back;
+ *   - the scripts. Nothing extra: the script-rate pacing accumulates ticks,
+ *     so at 8/9 a field it steps every fourth field, as it steps every
+ *     other one at 60.
+ *
+ * Twice the frames in the same guest second needs twice the CPU headroom,
+ * so asked for 120 the gate opens with the clock at C2_120_CPU_PCT, VSync's
+ * timeout widened four times to match, and it stays there at 60 (see
+ * c2_60_gate_cpu). Falling back is a staircase, not a cliff: a
+ * window that fails at 120 - the host behind, or frames not staying on one
+ * field - drops to the 60 FPS mode with the gate still open, retried after
+ * C2_120_RETRY_MS (doubling); only a failure at 60 closes the gate. Netplay
+ * and frame interpolation never engage it, and demo playback closes the
+ * gate as before. Every word is checked (c2_120_signature_ok) on top of the
+ * 60 FPS anchors, and everything reverts with the gate. */
